# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 5 of the Tutorial (Part 2)

[Bo2's Example 3.2 (Adder or Summing)]

ea,3,0,va
eb,2,0,vb
r31,3,1,r1
r21,2,1,r1
r1o,1,o,r2
o,0,1,o

analysis: dc
note: The summing amplifier, or adder: find vo, which comes back -(r2/r1)*(va+vb).
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-example-3-2-adder-or-summing-25.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[AS2's Figure 5.21 (Adder or Summing)]

e1,b,0,v1
e2,c,0,v2
e3,d,0,v3
r1,b,a,r1
r2,c,a,r2
r3,d,a,r3
rf,a,o,rf
o,0,a,o

analysis: dc
note: Find vo for the three-input adder: ask Evaluate for expand(vo), exactly as on the calculator, and it comes back -rf*v1/r1 - rf*v2/r2 - rf*v3/r3.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/as2s-figure-5-21-adder-or-summing-27.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


