[AS2's Figure 5.24 (Subtractor)]

e1,d,0,v1
e2,c,0,v2
r1,d,a,r1
r3,c,b,r3
r2,a,o,r2
r4,b,0,r4
o,b,a,o

analysis: dc
note: Find vo when r2 = r1 and r3 = r4: it reduces to v2 - v1. The same circuit with the two equalities the problem gives, put in Expert Mode's Add conditions so the answer comes back already reduced.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/as2s-figure-5-24-difference-or-differential-34.jpg
conditions: r2 = r1
conditions: r3 = r4
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[AS2's Example 5.7 (the v1 factor)]

e1,d,0,v1
e2,c,0,v2
r1,d,a,r1
r3,c,b,r3
r2,a,o,r2
r4,b,0,r4
o,b,a,o

analysis: dc
note: A design problem: the output must be -5*v1 + 3*v2. Conditions on the inputs rather than the resistors. With v1 = 1 and v2 = 0, vo is the v1 factor, -r2/r1. This factor has to equal -5 for the design asked for.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/as2s-figure-5-24-difference-or-differential-34.jpg
conditions: v1 = 1
conditions: v2 = 0
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[AS2's Example 5.7 (the v2 factor)]

e1,d,0,v1
e2,c,0,v2
r1,d,a,r1
r3,c,b,r3
r2,a,o,r2
r4,b,0,r4
o,b,a,o

analysis: dc
note: The v2 factor of the same design, via v1 = 0 and v2 = 1. This factor has to equal 3. Solving the two together for r2 and r4 gives r2 = 5*r1 and r4 = r3.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/as2s-figure-5-24-difference-or-differential-34.jpg
conditions: v1 = 0
conditions: v2 = 1
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[AS2's Example 5.7 (checking the design)]

e1,d,0,v1
e2,c,0,v2
r1,d,a,10'k
r3,c,b,20'k
r2,a,o,50'k
r4,b,0,20'k
o,b,a,o

analysis: dc
note: Verify the design: the same circuit with the book's values in place — r1 = 10k, r2 = 50k, r3 = 20k, r4 = 20k. vo comes back 3*v2 - 5*v1, as required.
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


